omega-effect-differential-rotation-0c3b6.intuitive_summary:
A twisting magnetic field (
$B_p ∇$
) in a rotating fluid (
$Ω$
) generates an azimuthal magnetic field (
$
B_{ϕ}$
) that grows over time (
$\
partial B_{ϕ}\
/\
partial t$
).

\\lambda.description:
The spatial period of the wave, the distance over which the wave's shape repeats. It is related to the wave number by 

\f$ \lambda = \frac{2\pi}{|k|} 

\f$. A negative wave number does not directly imply a negative wavelength, as wavelength is conventionally a positive distance.
